IMPORT prelude

§ `Fact schema (verbatim from inputs/schema.md, so this file is self-contained)`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                         IS A NUMBER

§§ `Supporting helpers (verbatim from inputs/schema.md — called, never redefined)`

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

§ `covered — one helper per policy clause, combined at the bottom`

§§ `Section 1.1(2) — the premium has been paid`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`premium paid` MEANS isJust (claim's `premium paid month`)

§§ `Section 1.3 — wellness-visit condition: satisfied on time, or still pending`

-- Satisfied: written confirmation supplied no later than month 7, of a wellness
-- visit, with a qualified provider, that itself occurred no later than month 6.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit condition satisfied` MEANS
       `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7
   AND `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`)      6
   AND (claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`)

-- Still pending: no written confirmation has been supplied yet, and the
-- 7-month deadline for supplying it has not yet passed as of the
-- hospitalization. A confirmation that HAS been supplied is no longer
-- "pending" -- it is judged directly against the deadline above, whether
-- timely or not.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit condition still pending` MEANS
       isNothing (claim's `written confirmation month`)
   AND (claim's `hospitalization month`) AT MOST 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit condition met or pending` MEANS
       `wellness visit condition still pending`  claim
   OR  `wellness visit condition satisfied`      claim

§§ `Section 1.2 — cancelation`

-- Cancelation occurs on fraud, on misrepresentation (the schema has no
-- separate field for "material withholding of information", so the
-- `misrepresentation month` field is read as standing for that whole
-- disjunct too), on a definitive (no-longer-pending) failure of the
-- Section 1.3 condition, or on the term simply running out.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy canceled` MEANS
       isJust (claim's `fraud month`)
   OR  isJust (claim's `misrepresentation month`)
   OR  NOT (`wellness visit condition met or pending` claim)
   OR  (claim's `hospitalization month`) GREATER THAN (claim's `policy term months`)

§§ `Section 1.1 — the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect` MEANS
       (claim's `agreement signed`)
   AND `premium paid` claim
   AND `wellness visit condition met or pending` claim
   AND NOT (`policy canceled` claim)

§§ `Section 1.1 — only a hospitalization for sickness or accidental injury is within scope`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`covered peril` MEANS
  CONSIDER (claim's `hospitalization ground`)
    WHEN Sickness             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Accidental injury`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN Neither              THEN FALSE

§§ `Section 2.1(1)-(4) — activity exclusions`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization arose from an excluded activity` MEANS
       `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Skydiving
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Military service`
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) Firefighting
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's `causes`) `Police service`

§§ `Section 2.1(5) — age exclusion`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`age exclusion applies` MEANS (claim's `age at hospitalization`) AT LEAST 80

§§ `Section 3.2.1 — arbitration as a condition precedent to liability, where a dispute has arisen`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration commenced timely` MEANS
  CONSIDER (claim's `unable to settle month`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST u  THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (u PLUS 3)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`dispute condition satisfied` MEANS
       NOT (claim's `dispute arisen`)
   OR  (    `arbitration commenced timely` claim
        AND (claim's `valid arbitration award issued`))

§§ `Section 3.2.1 — no recovery until 60 days (approximated as 2 months) after written proof of claim is submitted`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`recovery not premature` MEANS
  CONSIDER (claim's `recovery sought month`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST r  THEN
      CONSIDER (claim's `written proof of claim month`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST p  THEN r AT LEAST (p PLUS 2)

§ `covered`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE covered IF
       `policy in effect` claim
   AND `covered peril` claim
   AND NOT (`hospitalization arose from an excluded activity` claim)
   AND NOT (`age exclusion applies` claim)
   AND `dispute condition satisfied` claim
   AND `recovery not premature` claim
